From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 15:27:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Show the quote when the quoted message is an extended text

A reply shows the message it quotes as "> " lines, but only if the
quoted message is a plain Conversation. When the quoted message was
itself a reply, carried a mention or a link preview, it is an
ExtendedTextMessage, and the quote was dropped without a trace.

Fall back to the ExtendedTextMessage's text.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Submitted [https://github.com/hoehermann/purple-gowhatsapp/pull/297]
---
 handle_message.go | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/handle_message.go b/handle_message.go
index d40f754..ecb2af7 100644
--- a/handle_message.go
+++ b/handle_message.go
@@ -155,8 +155,13 @@ func (handler *Handler) handle_message(message *waE2E.Message, info types.Messag
 			ci := etm.ContextInfo
 			if ci != nil {
 				cm := ci.QuotedMessage
-				if cm != nil && cm.Conversation != nil {
-					quotelines := strings.Split(*cm.Conversation, "\n")
+				// the quoted message may itself be an extended text (a reply, a mention or a link)
+				quoted := cm.GetConversation()
+				if quoted == "" {
+					quoted = cm.GetExtendedTextMessage().GetText()
+				}
+				if quoted != "" {
+					quotelines := strings.Split(quoted, "\n")
 					text = "> " + strings.Join(quotelines, "\n> ") + "\n"
 				}
 			}
